The Track B check does not survive. Proposition 10 offers a polynomial scan, but on arbitrary graphs the “compact” route is still the same neighborhood inspection and exceeds the 300-operation cap before the answer space becomes guess-resistant. The only genuinely compact paper-backed cases—paths and hypercubes—are already given by direct formulas, so their mechanical and compact routes are comparable. I’m documenting this as an H rejection (with the general strategy-tree candidate also failing the witness/output constraints), rather than manufacturing hardness through an unrelated encoding.
