/tmp/burning-paper.oKOg4Q/src/arxiv.tex:377:        \item If $\Delta(G) \geq n-2$, then Burner's strategy is to first play a vertex of degree at least $n-2$. In the second rounds, all vertices but at most one are burned, thus Staller has no other option but to play the remaining unburned vertex and so $\bg(G) \leq 2$. Since $G \neq K_1$, $\bg(G) \geq 2$.
