/tmp/burning-paper.oKOg4Q/src/arxiv.tex:509:The upper bound in Proposition \ref{prop:sum-S-game} is tight for example for complete graphs. Note that the lower bound is achieved for $G=K_2$. However, using Proposition \ref{prop:characterize-1-2} and a simple case analysis, one can deduce that if $n \geq 5$, then $\bg'(G) + \bg'(\overline{G}) \geq 6$, which is tight for example for $G = K_{1, n-1}$.
