codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on Proposition 10 of the [Burning game paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.11328).

Key results:

- Exact inverse-generated, unique winning first moves.
- All local gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- 400 additional preset/seed stress instances passed.
- Eight adversary attacks fail 0/8, including the previously successful largest-two-neighborhood attack.
- Exact shipping guess probability: \(31^{-48}\approx2.60\times10^{-72}\).
- Standard algorithm: 74,524 operations on average.
- Compact symmetry route: 296 operations.
- Answer size: 50 characters, 48 elements.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.11328/gen_2409_11328.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.11328/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.11328/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.11328/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.11328/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.11328/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The remaining blocker is external: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every harness call. Consequently, the transcripts correctly record errors and zero scored attempts; no external hardness verdict is claimed. A replenished OpenRouter key is required before submission.
