The existing draft has a real audit issue: it treats the common relabelling as hidden scaffolding, but the statement never promises that relation, while the canonical key treats cross-game labels as meaningful. I’m tightening the contract so the shared bijection is part of the instance and adjusting the guess distribution to sample only words consistent with an injective relabelling. Before doing so, I’m also testing the construction-aware attack the earlier panel omitted: single-pair color refinement / graph-isomorphism recovery.
