   111	
   112	OUTPUT ENCODING
   113	Use the alphabet '0123456789abcd': its character at position v denotes vertex v.
   114	Output exactly one 4-character word. Character i is the move for target
   115	game i; there are no separators or spaces inside the word.
   116	Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags, as that exact word.
   117	Example shape for 4 entries: <answer>0123</answer>
   118	The example illustrates encoding only and is not an answer to this instance.
   119	Output nothing else inside the tags.
   120	```
   121	
   122	The answer is `5076`. `verify(inst, "5076")` returns `(True, "ok")`.
   123	Changing the first symbol gives `verify(inst, "0076") ==
   124	(False, "entry 0 is not a three-round winning first move")`.
   125	
   126	## Difficulty presets
   127	
   128	| preset | vertices/game | games | profile layers | compact operations | status |
   129	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
   130	| demo | 14 | 4 | 4 | 116 | hand-solvable example |
   131	| easy | 18 | 48 | 4 | 192 | local gates pass; oracle unscored |
   132	| medium | 24 | 48 | 4 | 240 | local gates pass; oracle unscored |
   133	| **hard** | **31** | **48** | **4** | **296** | `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY`; oracle unscored |
   134	
   135	No preset was rejected: the external ladder never completed a scored call.
   136	`escalate()` returns `"cap_bound"` beyond hard because one more vertex would push
   137	the measured compact route past 300 operations.
   138	
   139	## Gate results
   140	
   141	| gate | result | measured evidence |
   142	|---|---|---|
   143	| G1 | pass | 12 preset/seed instances; 444 unique-winner audits; 168 literal game-tree cross-checks |
   144	| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
   145	| G3 | pass | 48-symbol fenced/prose response round-tripped |
   146	| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; exact probability `31^-48 = 2.598e-72` |
   147	| G5 | pass | exactly 1 valid shipping word; strongest failed attack used 2,048 restarts total |
   148	| G6 | pass | nine attacks, each 0/8; Proposition 10, pairwise 1-WL, and compact transport each 8/8 |
   149	| G7 | pass | doubled `n=62` instance built and verified |
   150	| G8 | pass | 80 invariance checks, 80 carried witnesses, 20/20 distinct unrelated keys |
   151	| G9(c) | pass | 50 serialized characters/tokens (conservative one-character-per-token bound), 48 atoms, 296 operations |
   152	
   153	## Oracle loop and G9 diagnostics
   154	
   155	The harness made four calls per arm before correctly stopping. Each was an HTTP 403
   156	key-limit error, so the scored denominator is zero.
   157	
   158	| bare preset | seed | model | solved | why |
   159	|---|---:|---|---|---|
   160	| easy | 1499081598 | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | OpenRouter total key limit |
   161	| easy | 1348122602 | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | OpenRouter total key limit |
   162	| easy | 2144862522 | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | OpenRouter total key limit |
   163	| easy | 891109793 | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | OpenRouter total key limit |
   164	
   165	| arm | preset | solved/attempts | raw calls | conclusion |
   166	|---|---|---:|---:|---|
   167	| bare | easy | 0/0 | 4 errors | no hardness verdict |
   168	| structural hint | hard | 0/0 | 4 errors | diagnostic blocked |
   169	| placebo hint | hard | 0/0 | 4 errors | diagnostic blocked |
   170	
   171	`hinted - placebo` is undefined evidentially; the report stores `0.0` only because
   172	both scored denominators are zero. The hint's effect has not been measured.
   173	
   174	## Use
   175	
   176	```python
   177	from gen_2409_11328 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, parse_answer, render, verify
   178	
   179	inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["demo"])
   180	question = render(inst)
   181	answer = parse_answer(f"Result: <answer>{inst['answer']}</answer>")
   182	assert verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
   183	```
   184	
   185	From the repository root, after a valid bare hardening verdict:
   186	
   187	```bash
   188	bash scripts/emit.sh 2409.11328 20 hard
   189	```
   190	
   191	The module is deterministic, standard-library-only, performs no file or network IO,
   192	and prints only when executed as a script.
   193	
   194	## Caveats
   195	
   196	- The mandatory oracle evidence is absent because the OpenRouter key is exhausted.
   197	  The module is locally verified but must not be called externally hardened until
   198	  the bare and diagnostic runs complete.
   199	- The exact `P(guess)` uses a uniform prior over correctly sized words—one in-range
   200	  vertex per game. It does not model a solver that recognizes the reference/target
   201	  correlation; that informed route is measured separately at 296 operations.
   202	- The shared relabelling is benchmark scaffolding, not a theorem in the paper. The
   203	  objects and verifier remain native burning-game graphs, but the intended symmetry
   204	  is supplied by the generator.
   205	- The failing panel includes degree extremes, largest two-neighborhood, single-pair
   206	  degree matching, a one-layer shared-map guess, unchanged-label and cyclic-shift
   207	  ansatzes, and random restart. Pairwise 1-WL was tried and succeeds 8/8, so Track B
   208	  records it as a reference algorithm. A full individualization/refinement graph-
   209	  isomorphism package was not run because the cheaper 1-WL attack already solves.
   210	- `canonical_key` uses a multiset of rooted-reference/unrooted-target
   211	  Weisfeiler–Leman fingerprints and deliberately forgets the hidden cross-layer
   212	  alignment. It passed common and independent graph relabellings plus pair reorderings,
   213	  but it is not a complete canonical form for graph isomorphism.
   214	- Forty-eight output symbols are within the cap but still require careful
   215	  transcription. The fixed-width encoding keeps the serialized answer to 50
   216	  characters.

